BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jan-detectors@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260102
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Test smoke and CO detectors
DESCRIPTION:Test every smoke and carbon monoxide detector. Replace the batt
 eries. Replace any detector over 10 years old.\n\nWhy: sensors degrade wit
 h age whether or not the unit still chirps\, and a detector past its rated
  life can pass a button test and still fail in a real fire.\n\nDetails: ht
 tps://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#jan-detectors\n\nGeneral mainte
 nance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, 
 or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jan-freeze-prep@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260111
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Freeze prep\, find your water shutoff
DESCRIPTION:Locate your main water shutoff and make sure you can actually t
 urn it. Cover outdoor spigots.\n\nWhy: coastal plumbing is often run throu
 gh uninsulated exterior walls because it rarely needs to survive a freeze.
  When one comes\, knowing where the shutoff is turns a flooded house into 
 a wet floor.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#jan-
 freeze-prep\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licen
 sed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jan-attic-check@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260121
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Check the attic after winter rain
DESCRIPTION:Look for daylight through the roof deck\, damp or matted insula
 tion\, and water stains on the framing.\n\nWhy: a small roof leak shows up
  in the attic long before it shows up on your ceiling. Winter rain is the 
 easiest time to catch one.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.co
 m/guides/#jan-attic-check\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitu
 te for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-feb-termite-inspection@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260202
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Schedule the annual termite inspection
DESCRIPTION:Book it now\, before spring swarm season fills the schedule.\n\
 nWhy: Formosan and native subterranean termites are endemic across the Gul
 f Coast\, and damage is almost never covered by homeowners insurance. An a
 nnual inspection is the cheapest insurance you can buy.\n\nDetails: https:
 //gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#feb-termite-inspection\n\nGeneral m
 aintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contract
 or\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-feb-hvac-filter@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260211
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Replace the HVAC filter\, test the A/C
DESCRIPTION:Swap the filter and run the air conditioning briefly.\n\nWhy: f
 inding a cooling problem in February means an appointment. Finding it in J
 uly means a wait list\, a premium\, and a hot house.\n\nDetails: https://g
 ulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#feb-hvac-filter\n\nGeneral maintenance
  guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or yo
 ur insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-feb-caulk@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260220
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260221
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Walk the exterior and re-caulk
DESCRIPTION:Re-caulk gaps around windows\, doors\, and any penetration thro
 ugh the wall.\n\nWhy: caulk is the cheapest material on the house and the 
 first line against wind-driven rain. On the coast it fails in 2–4 years.
 \n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#feb-caulk\n\nGen
 eral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, co
 ntractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-mar-hvac-service@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260302
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Service the HVAC before cooling season
DESCRIPTION:Get a professional service call before the cooling season start
 s.\n\nWhy: down here the system runs eight or nine months a year\, roughly
  double the load it was rated against. Service is what buys back the years
  that heat takes off.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/gui
 des/#mar-hvac-service\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute f
 or a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-mar-gutters@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260310
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260311
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Clear the gutters\, check the downspouts
DESCRIPTION:Clear the gutters and confirm every downspout discharges away f
 rom the foundation\, not against it.\n\nWhy: water dumped at the foundatio
 n is the start of settling\, slab cracks\, and a wet crawlspace. All of th
 em expensive\, all of them avoidable with a splash block.\n\nDetails: http
 s://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#mar-gutters\n\nGeneral maintenanc
 e guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or y
 our insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-mar-grading@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260320
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260321
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Check the grading around the house
DESCRIPTION:Walk the perimeter after a hard rain. Look for settling\, crack
 s\, and standing water.\n\nWhy: the ground should fall away from the house
 . Gulf Coast soils shift\, and grading that worked at closing may not work
  three years later.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guide
 s/#mar-grading\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a li
 censed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-apr-swarm-season@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260402
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Swarm season\, watch for termites
DESCRIPTION:Watch for winged termites indoors and around lights. Check for 
 mud tubes along the slab\, piers\, and foundation walls.\n\nWhy: a swarm i
 s the one time termites are visible to you. Mud tubes mean an active colon
 y is already feeding on the house.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemainte
 nance.com/guides/#apr-swarm-season\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a
  substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance poli
 cy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-apr-wash-exterior@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260410
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260411
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Wash the exterior\, inspect the siding
DESCRIPTION:Wash the house down and inspect siding\, brick\, and soffits fo
 r damage or gaps.\n\nWhy: salt air and humidity feed mildew and rot\, and 
 washing is how you find the soft spot behind it. Open soffits are also how
  squirrels and wasps get into the attic.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthome
 maintenance.com/guides/#apr-wash-exterior\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\
 , not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insuran
 ce policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-apr-spigots-irrigation@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260420
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260421
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Check spigots and service irrigation
DESCRIPTION:Check hose bibs and outdoor spigots for leaks. Service the irri
 gation system if you have one.\n\nWhy: a spigot that weeps against the fou
 ndation all summer does quiet\, steady damage\, and shows up on the water 
 bill.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#apr-spigots
 -irrigation\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licen
 sed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-may-insurance-hurricane-prep@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260502
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Verify insurance\, season opens June 1
DESCRIPTION:Verify your coverage BEFORE the season starts: wind\, and flood
  if you carry it. Photograph every room and the full exterior for your cla
 im file. Trim limbs back from the roof.\n\nWhy: flood policies generally t
 ake 30 days to take effect\, so June 1 is already too late to start. Photo
 s taken before a storm are what get a claim paid after one.\n\nDetails: ht
 tps://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#may-insurance-hurricane-prep\n\
 nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\
 , contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-may-generator-supplies@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260510
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260511
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Test the generator\, restock supplies
DESCRIPTION:Start and load-test the generator. Restock water\, batteries\, 
 and fuel. Confirm shutters or plywood are on hand and actually fit your op
 enings.\n\nWhy: a generator that has sat with old fuel since last season w
 ill not start when you need it\, and plywood cut to the wrong window is pl
 ywood you cannot use.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/gui
 des/#may-generator-supplies\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substi
 tute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy term
 s.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-may-secure-exterior@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260520
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260521
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Inspect roof edges\, secure loose items
DESCRIPTION:Inspect soffit vents and roof edges. Secure sheds\, fencing\, a
 nd anything that becomes a projectile.\n\nWhy: most wind damage starts at 
 an edge. Once wind gets under the roof edge or through an open soffit\, it
  works on the whole roof.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com
 /guides/#may-secure-exterior\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a subst
 itute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy ter
 ms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jun-condensate-line@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260601
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260602
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Clear the A/C condensate drain line
DESCRIPTION:Flush the condensate drain line and check the overflow pan and 
 float switch.\n\nWhy: a clogged condensate line is one of the most common 
 causes of ceiling damage on the coast. The unit keeps running and quietly 
 drains into your drywall.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com
 /guides/#jun-condensate-line\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a subst
 itute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy ter
 ms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jun-condenser-coils@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260610
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260611
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Clean the condenser\, clear vegetation
DESCRIPTION:Clean the outdoor condenser coils and cut vegetation back two f
 eet on all sides of the unit.\n\nWhy: a coil that cannot breathe makes the
  compressor work harder in the hottest months\, which is exactly how a 12-
 year unit becomes an 8-year unit.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemainten
 ance.com/guides/#jun-condenser-coils\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not
  a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance po
 licy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jun-attic-ventilation@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260621
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Check attic ventilation and insulation
DESCRIPTION:Check that soffit and ridge vents are clear\, and measure insul
 ation depth.\n\nWhy: a poorly vented attic bakes the roof deck from undern
 eath and shortens shingle life\, on top of what it costs you in cooling.\n
 \nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#jun-attic-ventilat
 ion\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed insp
 ector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jul-leak-hunt@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260702
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Hunt for leaks
DESCRIPTION:Check under every sink\, behind every toilet\, and around the b
 ase of the water heater.\n\nWhy: slow leaks are found by looking\, not by 
 waiting. In this humidity a cabinet leak becomes mold long before it becom
 es a stain you notice.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/gu
 ides/#jul-leak-hunt\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for
  a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jul-crawlspace@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260711
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Inspect the crawlspace
DESCRIPTION:Inspect the crawlspace or under-house area for moisture\, pests
 \, and vapor barrier damage.\n\nWhy: it is the part of the house nobody lo
 oks at and the part humidity attacks hardest. Rot and pests both start dow
 n there.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#jul-craw
 lspace\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed i
 nspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jul-humidity@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260721
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Check indoor humidity
DESCRIPTION:Measure indoor relative humidity. Aim for 45–55%. Run a dehum
 idifier if you are above that.\n\nWhy: above 60% indoors you are growing m
 old and inviting dust mites\, whatever the thermostat says.\n\nDetails: ht
 tps://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#jul-humidity\n\nGeneral mainten
 ance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, o
 r your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-aug-peak-season-check@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260802
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Peak season\, re-check kit and plan
DESCRIPTION:Re-check your supply kit\, your documents\, and your evacuation
  plan. Confirm your insurance is still active and paid.\n\nWhy: this is th
 e peak of the season. A lapsed policy or an expired document is something 
 you want to find now\, not while you are packing.\n\nDetails: https://gulf
 coasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#aug-peak-season-check\n\nGeneral maintena
 nce guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or
  your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-aug-gutters-again@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Clear the gutters again
DESCRIPTION:Clear the gutters a second time.\n\nWhy: summer storms fill the
 m fast\, and a full gutter in a tropical downpour sends the whole roof's w
 ater straight down your wall.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance
 .com/guides/#aug-gutters-again\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a sub
 stitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy t
 erms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-aug-photograph-valuables@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260821
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Photograph big-ticket items
DESCRIPTION:Photograph big-ticket items and store the photos somewhere off-
 site or in the cloud.\n\nWhy: proof of ownership is what turns a claim int
 o a payment\, and it is worthless if it only exists on a phone that went w
 ith the house.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#au
 g-photograph-valuables\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute 
 for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-sep-dryer-vent@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Clean the dryer vent
DESCRIPTION:Clean the full dryer vent run\, not just the lint trap.\n\nWhy:
  dryer lint is a leading cause of house fires\, and coastal humidity makes
  it pack into the duct harder and faster.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthom
 emaintenance.com/guides/#sep-dryer-vent\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, 
 not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance
  policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-sep-roof-inspection@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Inspect the roof from the ground
DESCRIPTION:Inspect the roof from the ground with binoculars after the summ
 er storm run. Look for lifted\, curled\, or missing shingles.\n\nWhy: you 
 can see almost everything that matters from the driveway\, and nobody has 
 ever fallen off a driveway.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.c
 om/guides/#sep-roof-inspection\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a sub
 stitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy t
 erms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-sep-sump-drainage@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Test the sump pump\, clear drainage
DESCRIPTION:Test the sump pump if you have one. Clear drainage swales and d
 itches.\n\nWhy: a sump pump that has not run in months is a sump pump you 
 should not assume works. Blocked ditches move the water to your yard.\n\nD
 etails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#sep-sump-drainage\n\n
 General maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\,
  contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-oct-flush-water-heater@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Flush the water heater
DESCRIPTION:Drain and flush the tank to clear sediment.\n\nWhy: sediment in
 sulates the burner from the water and cooks the tank from the inside. Gulf
  Coast water heaters are already short-lived\; this is most of the differe
 nce between 8 years and 12.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.c
 om/guides/#oct-flush-water-heater\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a 
 substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance polic
 y terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-oct-weatherstripping@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Check weatherstripping and seals
DESCRIPTION:Check weatherstripping\, door sweeps\, and the attic hatch seal
 .\n\nWhy: those gaps are your largest uncontrolled air exchange\, which on
  the coast means you are paying to dehumidify the outdoors.\n\nDetails: ht
 tps://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#oct-weatherstripping\n\nGeneral
  maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contra
 ctor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-oct-chimney@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Service the fireplace or chimney
DESCRIPTION:Service the fireplace or chimney before first use.\n\nWhy: an u
 nused flue collects nests\, debris\, and moisture damage over a long warm 
 season.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#oct-chimn
 ey\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspe
 ctor\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-nov-filter-heat-test@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Replace the filter\, test the heat
DESCRIPTION:Replace the HVAC filter and run the heat once.\n\nWhy: the burn
 er or heat strips have sat unused since spring. Better to smell the dust b
 urn off in November than to find a dead system during a cold snap.\n\nDeta
 ils: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#nov-filter-heat-test\n\n
 General maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\,
  contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-nov-gutters-fascia@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:2
SUMMARY:Clear gutters\, check fascia and trim
DESCRIPTION:Clear the gutters after leaf drop. Check the fascia and trim fo
 r rot.\n\nWhy: fascia is where a gutter that overflowed all year finally s
 hows the damage\, and rotten fascia is how the gutter comes off in the nex
 t storm.\n\nDetails: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#nov-gutt
 ers-fascia\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licens
 ed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
